\subsection{Method \code{run_spls()}}{
Run unsupervised multi-omics integration using block.sPLS.

This function wraps \code{mixOmics::block.spls} to perform unsupervised multi-block sparse PLS.
It is suitable when there is no grouping variable and the user wants to explore the covariance
structure across multiple omics data sets.
Note that \code{mixOmics::block.spls} requires a numeric response matrix, so one omics block
must be designated as the response block through the \code{Y_block} parameter (passed to \code{indY}).
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{trans_multiomics$run_spls(
  ncomp = 2,
  Y_block = NULL,
  keepX = NULL,
  design = NULL,
  mode = "regression",
  scale = TRUE,
  ...
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{ncomp}}{default 2; the number of components.}

\item{\code{Y_block}}{default NULL; the index or name of the omics block used as the response (\code{indY}).
If NULL, the last block in \code{data_list} is used.}

\item{\code{keepX}}{default NULL; a list of variable numbers to select per block per component (including the response block,
as \code{mixOmics} ignores keepY when \code{indY} is used). If NULL, all features are retained (full model).}

\item{\code{design}}{default NULL; the design matrix. If NULL, use \code{self$design}; if still NULL, create with \code{set_design()}.}

\item{\code{mode}}{default "regression"; the PLS mode. One of "regression", "canonical", "invariant", "classic".}

\item{\code{scale}}{default TRUE; whether to scale the data.}

\item{\code{...}}{other parameters passed to \code{mixOmics::block.spls}.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
