\subsection{Method \code{tune_model()}}{
Tune the DIABLO model to select the optimal number of variables to select (keepX).

This function wraps \code{mixOmics::tune.block.splsda} (or \code{tune.block.spls}) to perform
cross-validation and identify the optimal \code{keepX} per block per component.
The optimal parameters are stored in \code{best_keepX} for use in the final model.
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{trans_multiomics$tune_model(
  method = "block.splsda",
  ncomp = 2,
  test_keepX = NULL,
  folds = 10,
  nrepeat = 1,
  dist = "centroids.dist",
  seed = NULL,
  ...
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{method}}{default "block.splsda"; the tuning method. Currently only "block.splsda" is supported,
as \code{mixOmics} provides no tune function for unsupervised block.spls.}

\item{\code{ncomp}}{default 2; the number of components to tune.}

\item{\code{test_keepX}}{default NULL; a list of candidate keepX values per block.
If NULL, an adaptive grid (5\%, 10\% and 20\% of the feature number of each block) is used.}

\item{\code{folds}}{default 10; the number of folds for cross-validation.
Must not exceed the smallest class size of \code{Y}.}

\item{\code{nrepeat}}{default 1; the number of repeats. Increase to 10-50 for robust results.}

\item{\code{dist}}{default "centroids.dist"; the prediction distance for DA methods.}

\item{\code{seed}}{default NULL; an integer used to set the random seed before cross-validation for reproducible results.}

\item{\code{...}}{other parameters passed to \code{mixOmics::tune.block.splsda}.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
\subsection{Returns}{
\code{self} (invisible), enabling chained calls; \code{tune_result} and \code{best_keepX} are stored in the object.
}
